## Rules

- **Never** hardcode model names — always use `models.config.ts` tier aliases
- **Always** validate LLM output with Zod — never use raw text as structured data
- **Always** version prompts — log prompt version with every LLM call
- **Always** track token usage and estimated cost per call
- **Never** ship a prompt change to production without running evals first
- **Always** handle the "empty context" case in RAG — do not hallucinate when context is thin
- Use `temperature: 0.1–0.2` for structured extraction, `0.7–0.9` for creative generation
- Use `CHEAP` tier for classification and routing decisions; `REASONING` only when necessary
- **Always** set `max_tokens` explicitly — never rely on API defaults
- Chunk documents at semantic boundaries (sentences/paragraphs), not arbitrary character counts
- Cache embeddings — never re-embed the same content twice
- Prefer local models for dev and sensitive data; cloud models for production reasoning tasks
